# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Debugging and tracing for the latest version of Samplomatic"
msgstr "Débogage et traçage pour la dernière version de Samplomatic"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Debugging and tracing"
msgstr "Débogage et traçage"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Debugging and tracing {#debugging-and-tracing}"
msgstr "Débogage et traçage {#debugging-and-tracing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function transforms an annotated circuit into a template circuit and samplex pair. In a complex circuit it can be hard to tell which box in the original circuit corresponds to which barriers in the template, or which nodes in the samplex DAG.\n"
msgstr "La fonction [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") transforme un circuit annoté en une paire circuit modèle et samplex. Dans un circuit complexe, il peut être difficile de savoir quelle boîte du circuit d'origine correspond à quelles barrières du modèle, ou à quels nœuds du DAG du samplex.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic provides two complementary tracing tools:\n"
msgstr "Samplomatic fournit deux outils de traçage complémentaires :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Barrier labels**: Every barrier in the template circuit carries a label that encodes its origin. These are always present regardless of whether `debug=True` is set.\n"
msgstr "**Étiquettes de barrière** : chaque barrière du circuit modèle porte une étiquette qui encode son origine. Elles sont toujours présentes, que `debug=True` soit défini ou non.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Trace info on samplex nodes**: When [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") is called with `debug=True`, every samplex node carries a `TraceInfo` object linking it back to the box or boxes that produced it.\n"
msgstr "**Informations de trace sur les nœuds du samplex** : quand [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") est appelé avec `debug=True`, chaque nœud du samplex porte un objet `TraceInfo` qui le relie à la ou aux boîtes qui l'ont produit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both tools are most useful when boxes carry a [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation, which attaches a `ref` string to the box. Alternatively, [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") references are also attached.\n"
msgstr "Les deux outils sont particulièrement utiles quand les boîtes portent une annotation [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\"), qui attache une chaîne `ref` à la boîte. Les références [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") sont également attachées.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tag boxes {#tag-boxes}"
msgstr "Étiqueter les boîtes {#tag-boxes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation attaches a `ref` string to a box. The `ref` then appears in barrier labels and in trace information on samplex nodes.\n"
msgstr "Une annotation [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") attache une chaîne `ref` à une boîte. Le `ref` apparaît ensuite dans les étiquettes de barrière et dans les informations de trace des nœuds du samplex.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following example circuit has three boxes: two tagged CX boxes on disjoint qubit pairs, and an untagged right-dressed measurement box. The second CX box also carries an [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation — both its `tag` ref and its noise `ref` will appear in the barrier labels. The two CX boxes cover different qubits, which enables the samplex optimizer to merge their propagation nodes into shared nodes. This is shown in the trace information section.\n"
msgstr "Le circuit d'exemple suivant comporte trois boîtes : deux boîtes CX étiquetées sur des paires de qubits disjointes, et une boîte de mesure à habillage droit sans étiquette. La seconde boîte CX porte aussi une annotation [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") — son `tag` ref comme son `ref` de bruit apparaîtront dans les étiquettes de barrière. Les deux boîtes CX couvrent des qubits différents, ce qui permet à l'optimiseur de samplex de fusionner leurs nœuds de propagation en nœuds partagés. Cela est montré dans la section sur les informations de trace.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barrier labels in the template circuit {#barrier-labels-in-the-template-circuit}"
msgstr "Étiquettes de barrière dans le circuit modèle {#barrier-labels-in-the-template-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calling [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") on the circuit above produces a template whose barriers carry identifying labels. Each label has the form `{side}{scope}@{key=value&...}`:\n"
msgstr "Appeler [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") sur le circuit ci-dessus produit un modèle dont les barrières portent des étiquettes d'identification. Chaque étiquette a la forme `{side}{scope}@{key=value&...}` :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Side**: `L` = left-dressing boundary, `M` = inner box content boundary, `R` = right-dressing boundary.\n"
msgstr "**Côté** : `L` = frontière d'habillage gauche, `M` = frontière du contenu interne de la boîte, `R` = frontière d'habillage droit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Scope**: An integer index (or underscore-separated list for nested boxes) that distinguishes multiple boxes at the same nesting level.\n"
msgstr "**Portée** : un indice entier (ou une liste séparée par des tirets bas pour les boîtes imbriquées) qui distingue plusieurs boîtes au même niveau d'imbrication.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Annotations**: An `@`-prefixed, `&`-separated list of `key=value` pairs derived from the box’s annotations. The `tag` key comes from a [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation and `inject_noise` comes from an [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation.\n"
msgstr "**Annotations** : une liste préfixée par `@` et séparée par `&` de paires `key=value` dérivées des annotations de la boîte. La clé `tag` provient d'une annotation [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") et `inject_noise` provient d'une annotation [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers from untagged boxes carry only the side and scope (for example, `L2`), with no `@` suffix.\n"
msgstr "Les barrières issues de boîtes sans étiquette ne portent que le côté et la portée (par exemple, `L2`), sans suffixe `@`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The barrier labels can also be extracted programmatically:\n"
msgstr "Les étiquettes de barrière peuvent aussi être extraites par programmation :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace information on samplex nodes {#trace-information-on-samplex-nodes}"
msgstr "Informations de trace sur les nœuds du samplex {#trace-information-on-samplex-nodes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing `debug=True` to [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") attaches trace information to every samplex node. Each node’s [`trace_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info\") attribute is a `TraceInfo` object whose `trace_refs` dictionary maps annotation keys (for example, `\"tag\"` and `\"inject_noise\"`) to sets of ref strings. Nodes without a corresponding box annotation have `trace_info=None`.\n"
msgstr "Passer `debug=True` à [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") attache des informations de trace à chaque nœud du samplex. L'attribut [`trace_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info\") de chaque nœud est un objet `TraceInfo` dont le dictionnaire `trace_refs` associe des clés d'annotation (par exemple, `\"tag\"` et `\"inject_noise\"`) à des ensembles de chaînes ref. Les nœuds sans annotation de boîte correspondante ont `trace_info=None`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw\") is called on a debug-built samplex, hovering over any node in the interactive graph reveals its `trace_refs` inside the hover tooltip.\n"
msgstr "Quand [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw\") est appelé sur un samplex construit en mode debug, survoler n'importe quel nœud du graphe interactif révèle ses `trace_refs` dans l'infobulle.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace information can also be inspected programmatically. Notice that some nodes carry references from both `'cx_ab'` and `'cx_cd'`. The samplex optimizer merged their parallel propagation nodes because the two boxes cover disjoint qubits and share a common predecessor from the right-dressed measurement box’s emission.\n"
msgstr "Les informations de trace peuvent aussi être inspectées par programmation. Remarque que certains nœuds portent des références à la fois de `'cx_ab'` et de `'cx_cd'`. L'optimiseur de samplex a fusionné leurs nœuds de propagation parallèles parce que les deux boîtes couvrent des qubits disjoints et partagent un prédécesseur commun issu de l'émission de la boîte de mesure à habillage droit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find all nodes that originate from a specific box, filter by the `\"tag\"` key:\n"
msgstr "Pour trouver tous les nœuds issus d'une boîte précise, filtre par la clé `\"tag\"` :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The samplex DAG {#the-samplex-dag}"
msgstr "Le DAG du samplex {#the-samplex-dag}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The samplex returned by [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") is a directed acyclic graph (DAG) where **edges denote register dependency**. That is, an edge from node A to node B means B must wait for A to have acted on the shared virtual registers before B is allowed to act. This is not a temporal ordering like the DAG of a quantum circuit. Instead, the graph flows from nodes responsible for generating randomizations to nodes responsible for synthesizing them as outputs.\n"
msgstr "Le samplex renvoyé par [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") est un graphe orienté acyclique (DAG) où **les arêtes dénotent une dépendance de registre**. Autrement dit, une arête du nœud A vers le nœud B signifie que B doit attendre que A ait agi sur les registres virtuels partagés avant de pouvoir agir. Ce n'est pas un ordre temporel comme le DAG d'un circuit quantique. Le graphe va plutôt des nœuds chargés de générer les randomisations vers les nœuds chargés de les synthétiser en sorties.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are three node types, each with a distinct visual style in the interactive plot:\n"
msgstr "Il existe trois types de nœuds, chacun avec un style visuel distinct dans le tracé interactif :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Shape  | Color         | Type                                                                                                                                                             | Role                                                            |\n"
"| ------ | ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Star   | Red           | [`SamplingNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-sampling-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode\")         | Instantiates new virtual registers from a distribution or input |\n"
"| Circle | Green         | [`EvaluationNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-evaluation-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode\") | Transforms, combines, or propagates virtual registers           |\n"
"| Bowtie | Blue / Purple | [`CollectionNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collection-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode\") | Reads registers and writes to `sample()` outputs                |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Forme  | Couleur       | Type                                                                                                                                                             | Rôle                                                            |\n"
"| ------ | ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Étoile | Rouge         | [`SamplingNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-sampling-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode\")         | Instancie de nouveaux registres virtuels à partir d'une distribution ou d'une entrée |\n"
"| Cercle | Vert          | [`EvaluationNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-evaluation-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode\") | Transforme, combine ou propage des registres virtuels           |\n"
"| Nœud papillon | Bleu / Violet | [`CollectionNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collection-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode\") | Lit des registres et écrit dans les sorties de `sample()`       |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution proceeds in three phases:\n"
msgstr "L'exécution se déroule en trois phases :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "All sampling nodes run first (in parallel).\n"
msgstr "Tous les nœuds d'échantillonnage s'exécutent en premier (en parallèle).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluation nodes run next, in topological order (parallel within each generation).\n"
msgstr "Les nœuds d'évaluation s'exécutent ensuite, dans l'ordre topologique (en parallèle au sein de chaque génération).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collection nodes run last (in parallel).\n"
msgstr "Les nœuds de collecte s'exécutent en dernier (en parallèle).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The graphviz layout reflects this. Sampling nodes appear at the top, collection nodes at the bottom.\n"
msgstr "La disposition graphviz reflète cela. Les nœuds d'échantillonnage apparaissent en haut, les nœuds de collecte en bas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hover tooltips {#hover-tooltips}"
msgstr "Infobulles au survol {#hover-tooltips}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every node in the interactive visualization shows a tooltip when you hover over it. The tooltip contains the following information:\n"
msgstr "Chaque nœud de la visualisation interactive affiche une infobulle quand tu le survoles. L'infobulle contient les informations suivantes :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Node class name** and its integer graph index.\n"
msgstr "**Nom de la classe du nœud** et son indice entier dans le graphe.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Register manifests**, which registers the node instantiates, reads from, writes to, and removes. These tell you how data flows between nodes.\n"
msgstr "**Manifestes de registres**, c'est-à-dire les registres que le nœud instancie, lit, écrit et supprime. Ils t'indiquent comment les données circulent entre les nœuds.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Node-specific details**, including the distribution type for sampling nodes, the operand for multiplication nodes, the template parameter indices for collection nodes, and so on.\n"
msgstr "**Détails propres au nœud**, y compris le type de distribution pour les nœuds d'échantillonnage, l'opérande pour les nœuds de multiplication, les indices de paramètres du modèle pour les nœuds de collecte, etc.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Trace refs** (only when `debug=True`), which are the annotation keys and ref strings that link the node back to its originating boxes.\n"
msgstr "**Trace refs** (uniquement avec `debug=True`), qui sont les clés d'annotation et les chaînes ref reliant le nœud aux boîtes dont il provient.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clicking the plot and then hovering over individual nodes is the fastest way to understand what a given node does without reading source code.\n"
msgstr "Cliquer sur le tracé puis survoler les nœuds un par un est le moyen le plus rapide de comprendre ce que fait un nœud donné sans lire le code source.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplex summary {#samplex-summary}"
msgstr "Résumé du samplex {#samplex-summary}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before examining the visualization, `print(samplex)` gives a quick text summary of the node count, required inputs, and promised outputs.\n"
msgstr "Avant d'examiner la visualisation, `print(samplex)` donne un résumé textuel rapide du nombre de nœuds, des entrées requises et des sorties promises.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect registers {#inspect-registers}"
msgstr "Inspecter les registres {#inspect-registers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing `keep_registers=True` to [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") retains the intermediate [`VirtualRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-registers-virtual-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister \"samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister\") objects that are live at the end of sampling, and stores them in `outputs.metadata[\"registers\"]`. Each register is a 2D array (shape `(num_subsystems, num_randomizations)`, with possible trailing gate-shape dimensions) of virtual group elements.\n"
msgstr "Passer `keep_registers=True` à [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") conserve les objets [`VirtualRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-registers-virtual-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister \"samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister\") intermédiaires qui sont actifs à la fin de l'échantillonnage, et les stocke dans `outputs.metadata[\"registers\"]`. Chaque registre est un tableau 2D (de forme `(num_subsystems, num_randomizations)`, avec d'éventuelles dimensions finales de forme de porte) d'éléments de groupe virtuels.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is useful for verifying that virtual gates were combined correctly, or for inspecting the raw Pauli or unitary samples before they are synthesized into rotation angles.\n"
msgstr "C'est utile pour vérifier que les portes virtuelles ont été combinées correctement, ou pour inspecter les échantillons bruts de Pauli ou unitaires avant qu'ils soient synthétisés en angles de rotation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can view the contents of the end-state of a particular register. In the following example, the register has type [`PauliRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-registers-pauli-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister \"samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister\"). See the `API documentation(/apidocs/index)`\\_\\_ for details about the storage format.\n"
msgstr "Tu peux afficher le contenu de l'état final d'un registre particulier. Dans l'exemple suivant, le registre est de type [`PauliRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-registers-pauli-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister \"samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister\"). Consulte la `API documentation(/apidocs/index)`\\_\\_ pour des détails sur le format de stockage.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How samplex nodes map to template parameters {#how-samplex-nodes-map-to-template-parameters}"
msgstr "Comment les nœuds du samplex correspondent aux paramètres du modèle {#how-samplex-nodes-map-to-template-parameters}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `outputs[\"parameter_values\"]` array returned by [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") has shape `(num_randomizations, N)`, where `N` matches `len(template.parameters)`. Each column corresponds to one parameter in the template circuit — the i-th column fills in `template.parameters[i]`.\n"
msgstr "Le tableau `outputs[\"parameter_values\"]` renvoyé par [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") a la forme `(num_randomizations, N)`, où `N` correspond à `len(template.parameters)`. Chaque colonne correspond à un paramètre du circuit modèle — la i-ème colonne renseigne `template.parameters[i]`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`CollectTemplateValues`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collect-template-values#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues\") collection nodes are the link between virtual registers and template parameters. Each such node holds index information that records which columns of the output array it writes to. This makes it possible to trace which virtual gate subsystems drive which template parameters.\n"
msgstr "Les nœuds de collecte [`CollectTemplateValues`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collect-template-values#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues\") font le lien entre les registres virtuels et les paramètres du modèle. Chacun de ces nœuds contient des informations d'indice qui enregistrent dans quelles colonnes du tableau de sortie il écrit. Cela permet de retrouver quels sous-systèmes de portes virtuelles pilotent quels paramètres du modèle.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the \\{Samplex inputs and outputs}`samplex-io` guide to learn how to bind the sampled parameter values to the template circuit and run experiments.\n"
msgstr "Consulte le guide \\{Samplex inputs and outputs}`samplex-io` pour apprendre à lier les valeurs de paramètres échantillonnées au circuit modèle et à exécuter des expériences.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automatic tagging {#automatic-tagging}"
msgstr "Étiquetage automatique {#automatic-tagging}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\"), the `add_tags` parameter automatically adds [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotations to all boxes. Three modes are available:\n"
msgstr "Quand tu utilises [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\"), le paramètre `add_tags` ajoute automatiquement des annotations [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") à toutes les boîtes. Trois modes sont disponibles :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`\"unique_instance\"`**: Assigns sequential `ref` (`t0`, `t1`, and so on) to boxes in circuit order. Every box gets a distinct `ref` regardless of its structure.\n"
msgstr "**`\"unique_instance\"`** : attribue des `ref` séquentiels (`t0`, `t1`, etc.) aux boxes dans l'ordre du circuit. Chaque box reçoit un `ref` distinct, quelle que soit sa structure.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`\"unique_box\"`**: Computes a structural hash of each box’s content and assigns the same `ref` to all structurally equivalent boxes. This is useful for grouping boxes by type rather than position.\n"
msgstr "**`\"unique_box\"`** : calcule un hachage structurel du contenu de chaque box et attribue le même `ref` à toutes les boxes structurellement équivalentes. C'est utile pour regrouper les boxes par type plutôt que par position.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`\"noise_ref\"`**: Copies the `ref` from each box’s [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation and only tags boxes that have one. This is useful when meaningful noise refs already exist.\n"
msgstr "**`\"noise_ref\"`** : copie le `ref` de l'annotation [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") de chaque box et ne marque que les boxes qui en ont une. C'est utile lorsque des noise refs pertinents existent déjà.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following example applies `\"unique_instance\"` and `\"unique_box\"` to a circuit whose two CX boxes are structurally equivalent. With `\"unique_instance\"`, each gets a distinct `ref`, while with `\"unique_box\"`, they share one.\n"
msgstr "L'exemple suivant applique `\"unique_instance\"` et `\"unique_box\"` à un circuit dont les deux boxes CX sont structurellement équivalentes. Avec `\"unique_instance\"`, chacune reçoit un `ref` distinct, alors qu'avec `\"unique_box\"`, elles en partagent un seul.\n"
